rce distributes a labelled training manifest ( 6499 6499 rows, the value in Table 1 ) and a separate 2786 2786 -row manifest without labels. Only the labelled manifest is ingested, so Butterfly’s n n counts labelled rows available rather than all rows shipped with the dataset. Tabular. Credit-G is the Statlog German Credit dataset [ Hofmann, 1994 ] (OpenML credit-g , id 31; German bank applicants, 20 20 attributes, good/bad-risk labels). Breast Cancer is the UCI Ljubljana breast-cancer recurrence dataset [ Zwitter and Soklic, 1988 ] . Madelon is the artificial NIPS 2003 feature-selection challenge dataset [ Guyon et al., 2004 ] ( 500 500 features, of which 480 480 are non-informative noise probes), which we use as a high-dimensional sparsity stress test. Time series. Electricity is the ELEC2 dataset [ Harries, 1999 ] from the Australian New South Wales electricity market ( 45,312 45{,}312 half-hourly records; binary up/down price movement). We construct lag-1/2/3 features on five series (23 features after expansion) and use a time-ordered rather than random split. Text. Ecommerce Text is the E-commerce text dataset of Gautam [2019] , a product-description corpus in four categories (Household, Books, Electronics, Clothing & Accessories), represented by unigram/bigram TF-IDF features. Image. Butterfly Image is the public Kaggle Butterfly Image Classification dataset [ DePie, 2023 ] ; each image is represented by simple grayscale-intensity statistics and histograms (26 dimensions, with a filename-hash fallback when the raw image is unavailable), not by pretrained-CNN embeddings. The classifier reaches only ≈ 0.19 \approx 0.19 test accuracy on this 75-class task — well above the 1 / 75 ≈ 0.013 1/75\approx 0.013 chance rate, but low in absolute terms, since the representation is deliberately weak. Because it is by a wide margin the lowest-accuracy task in the suite, we report all dataset counts both with and without Butterfly as a robustness check. Appendix C Full Result